ell.Philosophy &ManifestoWe believe technology should serve people's working day, not reshape it around a tool. The best automation is quiet: it removes a chore, works every time and is easy to understand. We would rather automate one workflow well than ten badly. And we believe clients should always own, and understand, what we build for them.We stand for small firms having the same smart tools as large ones. We stand for automation that people understand, own and trust. We stand against hype, black-box systems and contracts that lock clients in. We stand against software that replaces people's judgement without anyone checking it. Everything we build exists for one reason: to give people back time for the work they chose their profession for.PagesIntroductionIdentity SystemBack
